{"seq":39,"slug":"hidden-markov-models","title":"隐马尔可夫模型","stage":"DONE","category":"data-science","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models","rating":{"composite":4.1,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.8,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":5,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"隐马尔可夫模型-为看不见的状态序列建模\">隐马尔可夫模型：为看不见的状态序列建模</h1><p>很多真实数据是一串按时间排开的观测，但驱动它们的东西你看不见：语音波形背后是想说的音素，DNA 碱基背后是基因的功能区段，股市涨跌背后是市场的牛熊状态。隐马尔可夫模型（Hidden Markov Model, HMM）正是为这类问题设计的——它假设有一条你观测不到的「隐状态」序列在按马尔可夫链演化，而你每一步只能看到隐状态随机吐出的一个观测。HMM 要回答的，就是「看着这串观测，我能不能反推出背后那条隐状态链」。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 沿四条主线递进，把 HMM 从直觉一路讲到落地。</p>\n<p>第一条线是<strong>基础</strong>：先说清楚为什么需要一个专门的模型来处理带隐结构的序列，再把马尔可夫假设、隐状态、以及三元组 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=(A,B,\\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 的形式定义摆出来，最后用 Rabiner 的经典框架把 HMM 的全部任务归纳为「评估、解码、学习」三大问题——后面所有章节都是在解这三个问题。</p>\n<p>第二条线是<strong>推断</strong>（已知模型参数）：前向后向算法解决评估问题并给出所有中间量，Viterbi 解决「最可能的整条路径」，后验边缘则回答「每个时刻各状态的概率」。这三者共享同一套动态规划骨架，却服务于不同问题，务必分清。</p>\n<p>第三条线是<strong>学习</strong>（参数未知）：Baum-Welch 用推断章得到的期望量迭代地估计参数，它本质是 EM 算法在 HMM 上的特例；EM 推导一篇讲清楚它为什么单调收敛、M 步公式怎么来的；初始化与缩放一篇处理让理论落地的数值现实——下溢、局部最优、状态置换。</p>\n<p>第四条线是<strong>实践</strong>：从离散 HMM 扩展到连续（高斯）与半马尔可夫变体，回顾语音与生物信息学这两个把 HMM 用到极致的领域，最后诚实地划出 HMM 的能力边界——什么时候该用它，什么时候 CRF、RNN 或 Transformer 是更好的选择。</p>\n<p><strong>本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工</strong>：HMM 是<a href=\"../probabilistic-graphical-models/foundations/what-are-pgms\">概率图模型</a>中一类特殊的动态贝叶斯网络，图模型 hub 讲通用的表示与推断框架，本 hub 只深挖 HMM 这一条时间链的专用算法。它也是<a href=\"../time-series-analysis/ts-fundamentals/time-series-concepts\">时间序列分析</a>的一员，但时间序列 hub 关注 ARIMA、平稳性这类连续值预测，本 hub 关注离散隐状态推断。学习章的 EM 与<a href=\"../bayesian-data-analysis/foundations/posterior-inference\">贝叶斯数据分析</a>的后验推断同源，那个 hub 讲通用贝叶斯计算，这里只讲 HMM 里的点估计。如果你要检测序列里状态何时切换，<a href=\"../change-point-detection/foundations/why-change-point\">变点检测</a> hub 是姊妹主题。</p>\n<p><strong>推荐学习路径</strong>：完全新手按 基础 → 推断 → 学习 → 实践 顺序读，不要跳，因为学习章直接调用推断章的量。有概率图模型背景的读者可略读基础章，直接从前向后向进入。只想工程落地的读者可先读 基础章的三大问题一览，再跳到实践章的落地与边界，反查算法细节。</p>\n<p><strong>前置知识</strong>：条件概率与贝叶斯公式、离散随机变量、矩阵乘法、以及基本的动态规划思想。学习章会用到对数似然与拉格朗日乘子，但都会在文内展开。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础：把「隐状态序列」这件事说清楚","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-hmm","title":"为何隐马尔可夫模型：给看不见的状态序列一个模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/foundations/why-hmm"},{"seq":2,"slug":"markov-assumption","title":"马尔可夫假设与隐状态：HMM 的形式定义","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/foundations/markov-assumption"},{"seq":3,"slug":"three-problems","title":"三大问题：Rabiner 框架下的 HMM 全景","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/foundations/three-problems"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"inference","title":"推断：模型已知，反推隐状态","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/inference","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"forward-backward","title":"前向后向算法：把指数求和压成线性递推","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/inference/forward-backward"},{"seq":2,"slug":"viterbi","title":"Viterbi 解码：整条最优路径而非逐点最优","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/inference/viterbi"},{"seq":3,"slug":"posterior-marginals","title":"后验边缘与平滑：逐时刻的状态概率","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/inference/posterior-marginals"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"learning","title":"学习：只有观测，把参数估出来","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/learning","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"baum-welch","title":"Baum-Welch 算法：从无标注序列估参数","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/learning/baum-welch"},{"seq":2,"slug":"em-derivation","title":"EM 推导：为何 Baum-Welch 单调收敛","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/learning/em-derivation"},{"seq":3,"slug":"initialization-scaling","title":"初始化与数值缩放：让理论真正跑起来","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/learning/initialization-scaling"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice","title":"实践：从课本模型到真实系统","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"hmm-variants","title":"变体：连续发射、半马尔可夫与结构扩展","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/practice/hmm-variants"},{"seq":2,"slug":"hmm-applications","title":"应用：语音识别与生物信息学两大主场","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/practice/hmm-applications"},{"seq":3,"slug":"hmm-in-practice","title":"落地与边界：库、选状态数、以及何时别用 HMM","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/hidden-markov-models/practice/hmm-in-practice"}]}]}